  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The method's reliance on LoD2 building data and street-view imagery means its applicability and accuracy depend on the local availability and resolution of these specific spatial datasets.",
      "what": "The study introduces a computational method to evaluate the vertical greening potential of individual building walls by integrating Level of Detail 2 (LoD2) building data with street-view imagery. Applied to Leipzig, Germany, the model calculates key physical factors like wall orientation and Window-to-Wall Ratio (WWR) to generate a composite index that prioritizes surfaces capable of mitigating urban heat stress.",
      "why": "It provides urban planners with a automated, wall-by-wall screening tool to target climate adaptation interventions, moving beyond generalized neighborhood-scale assessments to identify specific, high-impact surfaces for green facades."
    }
